<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Erzhu Rong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">493–530</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Erzhu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rong-people">Rong</a> was a frontier chieftain from northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanxi">Shanxi</a> and a general of the Northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-wei">Wei dynasty</a>. During the Six Garrisons rebellion he built a powerful army, and in 528, after the empress dowager Hu poisoned her son, he marched on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a>, enthroned Emperor Xiaozhuang and massacred some two thousand courtiers at Heyin. He dominated the state until Xiaozhuang killed him in 530.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/erzhu-rong.jpg" alt="Erzhu Rong" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%A4%AA%E5%8E%9F%E7%8E%8B%E5%B0%94%E6%9C%B1%E6%A6%AE%EF%BC%88%E5%8C%97%E5%8F%B2%E6%BC%94%E7%BE%A9%EF%BC%89.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
